#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:126
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Mutt"
msgstr "Instalação do Mutt"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:130
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>Mutt</application> ships with an HTML version of its manual, "
"but the text version is no longer provided because differences in the "
"formatting from different text browsers compared to the shipped version "
"caused complaints. To get a text file, the following are used in order of "
"preference: <application>lynx</application> with overstriking (backspaces) "
"for emphasis, <application>w3m</application> or "
"<application>elinks</application>: the latter two apparently provide plain "
"text. Plain text is generally preferred unless reading the HTML manual, so "
"the instructions below use <application>lynx</application> if available, or "
"else <application>links</application> to produce plain text."
msgstr ""
"O &quot;<application>Mutt</application>&quot; vem com uma versão "
"&quot;HTML&quot; do manual dele, mas a versão em texto não mais é fornecida "
"porque diferenças na formatação de diferentes navegadores de texto em "
"comparação com a versão enviada causaram reclamações. Para obter um arquivo "
"de texto, os seguintes são usados em ordem de preferência: "
"&quot;<application>lynx</application>&quot; com &quot;overstriking&quot; "
"(&quot;backspaces&quot;) para ênfase, "
"&quot;<application>w3m</application>&quot; ou "
"&quot;<application>elinks</application>&quot;: os dois últimos aparentemente"
" fornecem texto simples. O texto simples é geralmente preferido, a menos que"
" se leia o manual &quot;HTML&quot;, de forma que as instruções abaixo usam o"
" &quot;<application>lynx</application>&quot; se disponível, ou então o "
"&quot;<application>links</application>&quot; para produzir texto simples."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:145
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>Mutt</application> requires a group named <systemitem "
"class=\"groupname\">mail</systemitem>.  You can add this group, if it does "
"not exist, with this command (as the &root; user):"
msgstr ""
"<application>Mutt</application> exige um grupo chamado <systemitem "
"class=\"groupname\">mail</systemitem>. Você pode adicionar esse grupo, se "
"ele não existir, com este comando (como o(a) usuário(a) &root;):"

#.  nodump because group mail should have been created in lfs
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:151
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>groupadd -g 34 mail</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>groupadd -g 34 mail</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:154
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you did not install an <xref linkend=\"server-mail\"/>, you need to "
"modify the ownership of <filename class=\"directory\">/var/mail</filename> "
"with this command:"
msgstr ""
"Se não instalou um &quot;<xref linkend=\"server-mail\"/>&quot;, [então] você"
" precisa modificar a titularidade da propriedade de &quot;<filename "
"class=\"directory\">/var/mail</filename>&quot; com este comando:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:159
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>chgrp -v mail /var/mail</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>chgrp -v mail /var/mail</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:162
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Mutt</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale o &quot;<application>Mutt</application>&quot; executando os "
"seguintes comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:173
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To ensure that a plain text manual is created when using "
"<application>lynx</application> or to otherwise use "
"<application>links</application> to produce it (instead of "
"<application>elinks</application>), run the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Para garantir que um manual de texto simples seja criado ao usar o "
"&quot;<application>lynx</application>&quot; ou, caso contrário, para usar o "
"&quot;<application>links</application>&quot; para produzi-lo (em vez do "
"&quot;<application>elinks</application>&quot;), execute o seguinte comando:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:179
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed  -e 's/ -with_backspaces//' \\\n"
"     -e 's/elinks/links/'       \\\n"
"     -e 's/-no-numbering -no-references//' \\\n"
"     -i doc/Makefile.in</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sed -e 's/ -with_backspaces//' \\\n"
"     -e 's/elinks/links/'       \\\n"
"     -e 's/-no-numbering -no-references//' \\\n"
"     -i doc/Makefile.in</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:185
#, xml-text
msgid "Now configure and build the application:"
msgstr "Agora configure e construa o aplicativo:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:188
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr                           \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc                       \\\n"
"            --with-docdir=/usr/share/doc/mutt-&mutt-version; \\\n"
"            --with-ssl                              \\\n"
"            --enable-external-dotlock               \\\n"
"            --enable-pop                            \\\n"
"            --enable-imap                           \\\n"
"            --enable-hcache                         \\\n"
"            --enable-sidebar                        &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr                           \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc                       \\\n"
"            --with-docdir=/usr/share/doc/mutt-&mutt-version; \\\n"
"            --with-ssl                              \\\n"
"            --enable-external-dotlock               \\\n"
"            --enable-pop                            \\\n"
"            --enable-imap                           \\\n"
"            --enable-hcache                         \\\n"
"            --enable-sidebar                        &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:208
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr "Esse pacote não vem com uma suíte de teste."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:212
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:215
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>make install</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:228
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you used a DESTDIR method to only install to a temporary location as a "
"regular user (as part of a package management process), you will need to run"
" the following as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root </systemitem> user"
" after completing the real install:"
msgstr ""
"Se usou um método &quot;DESTDIR&quot; para instalar somente em um local "
"temporário como um(a) usuário(a) regular (como parte de um processo de "
"gerenciamento de pacotes), [então] você precisará executar o seguinte como "
"o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;"
" depois de concluir a instalação real:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:234
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>chown root:mail /usr/bin/mutt_dotlock &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod -v 2755 /usr/bin/mutt_dotlock</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>chown root:mail /usr/bin/mutt_dotlock &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod -v 2755 /usr/bin/mutt_dotlock</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:238
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"An info file is now installed, so you will also need to recreate the "
"<filename>/usr/share/info/dir</filename> as described when "
"<application>Texinfo</application> was installed in LFS."
msgstr ""
"Um arquivo &quot;info&quot; agora está instalado, de forma que você também "
"precisará recriar o &quot;<filename>/usr/share/info/dir</filename>&quot; "
"conforme descrito quando o &quot;<application>Texinfo</application>&quot; "
"foi instalado no LFS."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:248
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:251
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>sed ... -e 's/ -with_backspaces//' ...</command>: This turns off "
"the backspaces used for overstriking when <application>lynx</application> is"
" used, resulting in readable plain text when using <command>view</command>."
msgstr ""
"<command>sed ... -e 's/ -with_backspaces//' ...</command>: Isso desliga os "
"backspaces usados para overstriking quando o <application>lynx</application>"
" for usado, resultando em texto simples legível ao usar o "
"<command>view</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:257
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>sed ... -e 's/elinks/links/' ...</command>: This allows "
"<command>links</command> to be run instead of <command>elinks</command> "
"which is not in the book."
msgstr ""
"<command>sed ... -e 's/elinks/links/' ...</command>: Isso permite que o "
"<command>links</command> seja executado em vez do <command>elinks</command> "
"que não está no livro."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:263
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>sed ... -e 's/-no-numbering -no-references//' ...</command>: This "
"removes switches which are not understood by <command>links</command>."
msgstr ""
"<command>sed ... -e 's/-no-numbering -no-references//' ...</command>: Isso "
"remove chaves que não são entendidas pelo <command>links</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:268
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--enable-external-dotlock</parameter>: In some circumstances the "
"mutt-dotlock program is not created. This switch ensures it is always "
"created."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--enable-external-dotlock</parameter>: Em algumas circunstâncias,"
" o aplicativo &quot;mutt-dotlock&quot; não é criado. Essa chave garante que "
"ele seja sempre criado."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:274
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>--enable-pop</parameter>: This switch enables POP3 support."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--enable-pop</parameter>: Essa chave habilita o suporte a "
"&quot;POP3&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:278
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--enable-imap</parameter>: This switch enables IMAP support."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--enable-imap</parameter>: Essa chave habilita o suporte a "
"&quot;IMAP&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:282
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--enable-hcache</parameter>: This switch enables header caching."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--enable-hcache</parameter>: Essa chave habilita o "
"&quot;caching&quot; de cabeçalho."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:287
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--enable-sidebar</parameter>: This switch enables support for the"
" sidebar (a list of mailboxes). It is off by default, but can be turned on "
"by <command>:set sidebar_visible</command> in mutt (and off again with "
"':unset'), or it can be enabled in <filename> ~/.muttrc</filename>."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--enable-sidebar</parameter>: Essa chave habilita o suporte para "
"a barra lateral (uma lista de caixas de mensagens). Ela está desligado por "
"padrão, mas pode ser ligado por &quot;<command>:set "
"sidebar_visible</command>&quot; no &quot;mutt&quot; (e desligado novamente "
"com &quot;:unset&quot;), ou pode ser habilitado em "
"&quot;<filename>~/.muttrc</filename>&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:295
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-ssl</parameter>: This parameter adds SSL/TLS support from "
"openssl in POP3/IMAP/SMTP."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--with-ssl</parameter>: Esse parâmetro adiciona suporte a "
"&quot;SSL&quot;/&quot;TLS&quot; a partir do &quot;OpenSSL&quot; em "
"&quot;POP3&quot;/&quot;IMAP&quot;/&quot;SMTP&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:300
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--enable-autocrypt --with-sqlite3</option>: These two switches add "
"support for passive protection against data collection, using gnupg and "
"gpgme (gpgme is enabled by autocrypt). See <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.mutt.org/doc/manual/#autocryptdoc\">The Manual</ulink>."
msgstr ""
"<option>--enable-autocrypt --with-sqlite3</option>: Essas duas chaves "
"adicionam suporte para proteção passiva contra coleta de dados, usando "
"&quot;gnupg&quot; e &quot;gpgme&quot; (&quot;gpgme&quot; é habilitado por "
"&quot;autocrypt&quot;). Veja-se <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.mutt.org/doc/manual/#autocryptdoc\">O Manual</ulink>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:307
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--enable-gpgme</option>: This switch enables GPG support through the"
" GPGME package. Use this switch if you want GPG support in Mutt."
msgstr ""
"<option>--enable-gpgme</option>: Essa chave habilita o suporte a "
"&quot;GPG&quot; por meio do pacote &quot;GPGME&quot;. Use essa chave se você"
" quiser suporte a &quot;GPG&quot; no &quot;Mutt&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:313
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--enable-smtp</option>: This switch enables SMTP relay support."
msgstr ""
"<option>--enable-smtp</option>: Essa chave habilita o suporte a "
"retransmissão &quot;SMTP&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:318
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-idn2</option>: Use this parameter if both libidn and libidn2 "
"have been installed, and you wish to use libidn2 here."
msgstr ""
"<option>--with-idn2</option>: Use esse parâmetro se &quot;libidn&quot; e "
"&quot;libidn2&quot; tiverem sido instalados e você desejar usar "
"&quot;libidn2&quot; aqui."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:323
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-sasl</option>: This parameter adds authentication support "
"from <xref linkend=\"cyrus-sasl\"/> in POP3/IMAP/SMTP if they are enabled.  "
"Depending on the server configuration, this may not be needed for POP3 or "
"IMAP. However, it is needed for SMTP authentication."
msgstr ""
"<option>--with-sasl</option>: Esse parâmetro adiciona suporte de "
"autenticação a partir do &quot;<xref linkend=\"cyrus-sasl\"/>&quot; em "
"&quot;POP3&quot;/&quot;IMAP&quot;/&quot;SMTP&quot; se eles estiverem "
"habilitados. Dependendo da configuração do servidor, isso possivelmente não "
"seja necessário para &quot;POP3&quot; ou &quot;IMAP&quot;. No entanto, é "
"necessário para autenticação &quot;SMTP&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mutt.xml:330
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--with-gss</option>: This parameter adds authentication support for "
"Kerberos. If you need to use this support, make sure that <xref "
"linkend=\"mitkrb\"/> is installed and configured correctly, and then use "
"this option while building this package."
msgstr ""
"<option>--with-gss</option>: Esse parâmetro adiciona suporte à autenticação "
"para Kerberos. Se você precisar usar esse suporte, certifique-se de que "
"<xref linkend=\"mitkrb\"/> esteja instalado e configurado corretamente e, em"
" seguida, use essa opção ao construir esse pacote."

